-- ====================================================================
-- List every nozzle SPCO under /ANSI-NOZZLES with its bore
-- ====================================================================
-- RUN WITH:
--     $M C:\Users\A\Desktop\Projects\e3d_agent\Projects\JK-Project\output\list_nozzle_bores.mac
--
-- Note `$M`, NOT `$$MACRO`. `$$MACRO` is not an E3D command - it appears
-- nowhere in AVEVA's installed PMLLIB/PMLUI (0 hits across ~6900 files),
-- and aborts with "(47,50) CP: Meaningless symbol(s) in command line".
-- `$M <path>` is the real form, used throughout AVEVA's own PML.
--
-- Prints two lines per component: Name and Answer (the bore).
-- Copy the whole output back.
--
-- Only PML1 single commands are used: a bare path navigates, and
-- `Q NAME ANSWER` reports. No collect, no do/enddo - the Command Window
-- rejects those, and so would this file.

/150lb_Ansi_Flanged/AAZFBB011
Q NAME ANSWER
